# Force LF regardless of core.autocrlf — matters for git archive, which
# is how scripts/*.sh ship to the Linux VPS (see DEPLOY.md). Without this,
# Windows' core.autocrlf=true silently re-CRLFs shell scripts on archive
# even though the blob itself is stored as LF, breaking the "#!/bin/sh"
# shebang on the server (`bad interpreter`).
*.sh text eol=lf
